Package: lindos-core
Version: 1.0.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Lindos Team <team@lindos.dev>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), policykit-1 | polkitd, pkexec, xdg-utils, ca-certificates, curl | wget, gpg
Recommends: xfconf, flatpak, procps, systemd, lindos-tune, efibootmgr, mokutil, libnotify-bin
Suggests: lindos-desktop, lindos-settings, lindos-setup
Homepage: https://lindos.dev
Description: Lindos core library, privileged helper and command-line tools
 Lindos is a remaster of Linux Mint XFCE with a Windows-11-style desktop.
 This package ships the pure-Python 'lindos' module (paths, config, modes,
 browsers, hardware, helper client, theme, compat, ram, dualboot, update,
 session, installstate, updatestate), the polkit-guarded helper
 /usr/libexec/lindos/lindos-helper, the vendor browser installer (Edge/Chrome
 are downloaded from Microsoft's/Google's apt repositories — by the Lindos
 installer while it installs, or later on demand; their licences forbid
 shipping them on the ISO; Firefox is the system's .deb), the five mode
 definitions under /usr/share/lindos/modes and the CLIs lindos-mode, lindos-browser,
 lindos-config, lindos-ram, lindos-dualboot and lindos-update, plus the
 read-only lindos-update-notify.sh (login/6-hourly systemd --user timer
 toast when a Lindos component update is available; lindos-desktop ships
 the autostart entry that starts it on login).
 .
 lindos-dualboot restarts the PC once into an existing Windows installation
 (UEFI one-shot boot, or GRUB's one-shot boot on BIOS systems) for games and
 drivers that need a real Windows kernel — never an emulator, spoofer or VM
 trick, and it never edits Windows, BCD or firmware settings.
 .
 lindos-update keeps Lindos and the system underneath it up to date: it
 reports what a twice-daily root refresh found (lindos-update-refresh.timer
 writes /var/lib/lindos/update-state.json - it refreshes the package lists and
 simulates, and never installs anything), and installs the Lindos components
 or the whole plan only when asked, through the privileged helper (exact
 list, or a full upgrade that is checked against the plan you were shown and
 repaired afterwards; lindos-update-repair.service finishes an interrupted
 one at the next start). Packages come from the Lindos apt repository once
 one is configured (its source ships, switched off until a real key exists,
 in lindos-archive-keyring), or by sideloading local .deb files. An apt hook
 notes when an update needs a restart (/run/reboot-required); cleanup never
 removes the desktop or the running kernel. apt/dpkg are always present on a
 Debian/Ubuntu system (Priority: required/important), so no extra Depends are
 needed for this.
 .
 The installer records what it did in /var/lib/lindos/install-state.json
 (lindos.installstate, 'lindos-config install-state'); the first-boot units
 lindos-browser-firstboot.service and lindos-driver-firstboot.service are only
 silent retries for steps still pending there. is-live-session and
 oem-config-pending are the shared shell tests for 'running from the install
 medium' and 'the first-boot account wizard has not finished'; wait-for-network
 gives those retries a bounded wait for NetworkManager (network-online.target
 comes too early here, wait-online being masked); apt-serialise makes them take
 turns (a flock) and wait for a held dpkg lock (DPkg::Lock::Timeout) instead
 of failing at once, because apt does not queue by itself;
 'lindos-browser sync-default' (started at login by lindos-desktop) makes the
 browser chosen in Lindos Setup XFCE's preferred one once it is installed;
 lindos-live-inhibit.service keeps a live USB session from suspending during
 an installation.
 .
 No GTK dependency: the graphical parts live in lindos-setup / lindos-settings.
